                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "TACTICAL is what a crossover game between Metal Gear Solid: VR Missions and Hotline: Miami would feel like. The challenge is simple: Manipulate your soldier to eliminate robots from behind. The execution however is daunting: It's brutal, it's fast (some levels barely give you time to get in position before it's over), it requires failing mutilple times before you can come up with the proper soultion, and it is addictive. While this is, at its core, a puzzle game, you absolutely must have fast reflexes ad manual dexterity to be able to carry out the maneuvers needed to complete most missions.\n\nTACTICAL's design choices work in its favor; the minimalistic approach to graphics means information is clear and easy to digest on the fly (which is essential in this type of game). The chiptune music is repetitive and grating but, man, if that doesn't add to the massive tension felt whilst playing. Seriously: Alien Isolation doesn't get my heart rate and blood pressure as elevated as this game does. \n\nSpeaking of music, it and the sound effects levels can be adjusted, and the usual graphics options are avaialable. However, while the game does remember what level you're on, don't expect to be able to save within each board (you wouldn't be able to move fast enough to do so anyway). \n\nI suspect you already know without playing if this is up your alley. While it's not something I can handle for large amounts at a time, TACTICAL is a very welcome addition to my library. The only addition I'd like to see is Workshop support. Recommended.\n\n[quote]For more puzzle game reviews, news and everything puzzle-related, follow [url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/25928931-Puzzle-Lovers/]Puzzle Lovers[/url] and check out our [url=http://steamcommunity.com/groups/puzzlelovers]Steam Group[/url].",
